Fix for clingox UPSTREAM-ISSUES U53: clingo_control_register_backend ignores
clingo_backend_type_reify_steps and lets clingo_backend_type_reify_sccs turn
on step numbers too.

make_backend builds the reifier with reify_sccs as both of its flags, but
Reify::Reifier(std::ostream &, bool calculateSCCs, bool reifyStep) takes the
step flag second. The command line's --reify-steps takes another path
(OutputBase::fromFormat), which passes reifySteps and is correct. The C API
path now passes reify_steps. Against clingo v5.8.2; suitable for upstream.

diff --git a/libgringo/src/output/output.cc b/libgringo/src/output/output.cc
--- a/libgringo/src/output/output.cc
+++ b/libgringo/src/output/output.cc
@@ -845,7 +845,7 @@
     UBackend backend;
     switch (format) {
         case OutputFormat::REIFY: {
-            backend = gringo_make_unique<BackendAdapter<Reify::Reifier>>(std::move(out), reify_sccs, reify_sccs);
+            backend = gringo_make_unique<BackendAdapter<Reify::Reifier>>(std::move(out), reify_sccs, reify_steps);
             break;
         }
         case OutputFormat::INTERMEDIATE: {
